<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16850" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exhērēdo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		exheres, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>to disinherit.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fratrem exheredans te faciebat heredem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 2, 16, 41</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Clu. 48, 135</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Rosc. Am. 18, 52</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 4, 23, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 5,
				13, 32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 4,
				20</span></i>: liberos bonis, Q. Met. ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 1, 6,
				8</span></i> et saep.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to deprive the heir
				of</i> any thing: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut mensam ejus exheredaret,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					37, 2, 7, § 20</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
